---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
    title="Accessible icons and SVGs"
    metaDescription="Examples of accessible and inaccessible SVG icons and CSS generated icons."
    currentUrl="/screen-reader-examples/icons/"
  >
  <div class="my-8 mx-4 max-w-[80em] lg:mx-auto">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[40em]">
      <h1 id="skip-target">
        Accessible icons and SVGs
      </h1>
      <div>
        <p>Icons can be meaningful or decorative. Meaningful icons need an accessible name. Decorative icons should be hidden from assistive technologies so they do not add noise.</p>
        <p>Generated CSS content can be especially unpredictable. Different browser and screen reader combinations may expose generated text differently, so it is useful to test the patterns you use.</p>

        <h2>Meaningful inline SVG icons</h2>
        <p>These examples use the same SVG search icon. The first two give the icon an accessible name. The last one does not.</p>

        <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="Meaningful SVG icon examples">
          <figure class="icon-example">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <svg
                role="img"
                aria-labelledby="svg-title-search"
                class="demo-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              >
                <title id="svg-title-search">Search</title>
                <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
                <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Accessible:</strong> inline SVG with <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and <code>aria-labelledby</code>.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <svg
                role="img"
                aria-label="Search"
                class="demo-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              >
                <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
                <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Accessible:</strong> inline SVG with <code>role="img"</code> and <code>aria-label</code>.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <svg
                class="demo-icon"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              >
                <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.25" />
                <path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Not accessible:</strong> meaningful SVG with no accessible name.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <h2>Decorative inline SVG icons</h2>
        <p>If the visible text already explains the control or content, the icon is usually decorative. In that case, hide the SVG from screen readers.</p>

        <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="Decorative SVG icon examples">
          <figure class="icon-example">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <button type="button" class="icon-button-demo">
                <svg
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  focusable="false"
                  class="button-demo-icon"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                >
                  <path d="M5 12H19" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
                  <path d="M13 6L19 12L13 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
                </svg>
                Continue
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Accessible:</strong> button has text, and the decorative SVG has <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <button type="button" class="icon-button-demo">
                <svg
                  role="img"
                  aria-label="Arrow"
                  class="button-demo-icon"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                >
                  <path d="M5 12H19" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
                  <path d="M13 6L19 12L13 18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.25" />
                </svg>
                Continue
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Not ideal:</strong> the decorative icon has its own name, so some users may hear extra information.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <h2>CSS generated icons</h2>
        <p>These icons are created with the CSS <code>content</code> property. Screen reader support for generated content has changed over time and can vary by browser.</p>

        <div class="icon-example-grid" aria-label="CSS generated icon examples">
          <figure class="icon-example">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <span class="css-icon css-icon--circle">Profile status</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Accessible:</strong> the generated circle is decorative, and the visible text provides the name.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <div class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-only" role="img" aria-label="Next step"></div>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Accessible name added with ARIA:</strong> the visual arrow has no text, so the element needs a name.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example icon-example--warning">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <span class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-empty"></span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>Not accessible:</strong> the arrow is visual only and the element has no accessible name.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="icon-example">
            <div class="icon-example__demo">
              <span class="css-icon css-icon--arrow-alt">Continue</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>CSS generated alt text:</strong> the pseudo-element uses <code>content: "→" / ""</code> so the arrow can be treated as decorative where supported.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .icon-example-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .icon-example {
    border: 2px solid #bbc9f7;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .icon-example {
    border-color: #18399a;
  }

  .icon-example--warning {
    border-style: dashed;
  }

  .icon-example__demo {
    align-items: center;
    display: flex;
    min-height: 4rem;
  }

  .demo-icon {
    color: #54007b;
    height: 3rem;
    width: 3rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .demo-icon {
    color: #ade5f8;
  }

  .button-demo-icon {
    height: 1.5rem;
    width: 1.5rem;
  }

  .icon-button-demo {
    align-items: center;
    background-color: #033573;
    border: 4px solid transparent;
    color: white;
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo {
    background-color: #ade5f8;
    color: black;
  }

  .icon-button-demo:hover {
    background-color: transparent;
    border-color: #033573;
    color: #033573;
  }

  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo:hover {
    border-color: #ade5f8;
    color: #ade5f8;
  }

  .icon-button-demo:focus {
    outline: 2px solid black;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  :global(.dark) .icon-button-demo:focus {
    outline-color: white;
  }

  .css-icon {
    align-items: center;
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .css-icon--circle::before {
    background-color: #54007b;
    border-radius: 999px;
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    height: 1rem;
    width: 1rem;
  }

  :global(.dark) .css-icon--circle::before {
    background-color: #ade5f8;
  }

  .css-icon--arrow-only::before,
  .css-icon--arrow-empty::before,
  .css-icon--arrow-alt::before {
    color: #54007b;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-only::before,
  :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-empty::before,
  :global(.dark) .css-icon--arrow-alt::before {
    color: #ade5f8;
  }

  .css-icon--arrow-only::before,
  .css-icon--arrow-empty::before {
    content: "→";
  }

  .css-icon--arrow-alt::before {
    content: "→" / "";
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .icon-example-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
